Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] panvk: avoid DRM syncobj payload copies on kbase

Purpose: Use the runtime queue-submit fallback for Android native-buffer release
on kbase, whose binary sync type is not a DRM syncobj.
Source/Reference: local QueueSignalReleaseImageANDROID regression on p0178.
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2, Moto G86 5G.
Tested Kbase UAPI: Android 16 device; precise version not independently verified.
Mesa base range: pinned 5a07217f plus G615 series and jm-v7-wip through 0178,
with the experimental Kraid G615 FAU and IDVS overlay.
Dependencies: the above prepared tree; this is not part of the default series.
Validation test: tests/ahb/anb_release.c; see tests/README.md for scope and limits.

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_device.c
@@ -756,7 +756,10 @@ panvk_per_arch(CreateDevice)(VkPhysicalDevice physicalDevice,
    device->vk.shader_ops = &panvk_per_arch(device_shader_ops);
    device->vk.check_status = panvk_device_check_status;
    device->vk.get_timestamp = panvk_device_get_timestamp;
-   device->vk.copy_sync_payloads = vk_drm_syncobj_copy_payloads;
+#ifdef HAVE_PAN_KMOD_KBASE
+   if (!physical_device->kbase_node_path[0])
+#endif
+      device->vk.copy_sync_payloads = vk_drm_syncobj_copy_payloads;
 
    device->kmod.allocator = (struct pan_kmod_allocator){
       .zalloc = panvk_kmod_zalloc,
